<title>UK: Dutch 1992 gold sale was bigger than recent one.</title>
<headline>Dutch 1992 gold sale was bigger than recent one.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's announcement of sales by the Dutch central bank of 300 tonnes of gold compares with a larger total of 400 tonnes which it disposed of in an earlier sale in November-December 1992.</p>
<p>Earlier on Monday the bank announced sales which will be settled in February and March this year of 300 tonnes of gold from its reserves representing over 20 percent of its total holdings.</p>
<p>The sale in 1992 accounted for about 25 per cent of the bank's then total gold reserves, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Brian Spoors London newsroom +44 171 542 8058</p>
</text>
